      "math_academy_id": "q-112714",
      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=\\frac{3}{4}{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=4{b}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2}+3{b}_{3} \\\\  & =3{b}_{3}+2{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}(\\frac{3}{4}{b}_{3})-2\\cdot 3(-\\frac{1}{3}{b}_{1})-2(4{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2}-2{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
